    old "Instead, when she looked at him, she saw him still staring at the ground."
    new "Invece, quando lo guardò, lo vide ancora fisso a terra."

    old "His nails, digging into the arm rest of the couch."
    new "Le sue unghie, conficcate nel bracciolo del divano."

    old "Rage."
    new "Rabbia."

